  (text "Limb: 4 low-side channels. Muscle wire k runs from the Vin hole to hole Wk. W1/W2 and W3/W4 are the antagonist pairs." (at 20 18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid f9e985cd-b06b-46c8-921b-c3f8d72b0186))
  (text "Flyback diodes may be fitted DNP if the wire leads are short. Gate pull-downs keep every MOSFET off when the 74HC595 outputs are disabled." (at 20 22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid fe7992fe-7de8-4206-b0d5-d1e9fe9d4c5a))
  (text "AO3400A pins: 1 G, 2 S, 3 D (SOT-23)." (at 20 26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5d7cbb00-3aae-4ec9-9ae2-ab48fcc2ba93))
  (text "Gate guard (hardware, no software involved): CAC AC-couples the drive, RPD bleeds it, the BAT54 clamp restores the low level each cycle." (at 20 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 63eab7e4-005b-4eaa-b660-6e3cf8f1ac6f))
  (text "Normal pulses (up to ~250 us) pass with a few percent droop; a gate stuck high decays below threshold in ~3 ms (22 nF x 100 k). Use 100 nF with IRLZ34N." (at 20 34 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1c19f3e2-1de7-4a91-989d-8c0b604602ed))
)
